Backport the upstream system-keymap feature and its GTK settings wiring.
With use-system-keyboard-layout enabled, unhandled printable keys remain
key events instead of becoming unsolicited text commits. This prevents
Chrome from discarding letters after a tab shortcut, and preserves IME
composition handled by the engine.

Applies after Sekka's physical-keycode and serial backports to IBus 1.5.34.
The commits below are retained in upstream order, without functional changes.
See DEVELOPERS.md#aizome-and-ibus for scope, tests, known limits, and the
criteria for returning to the vanilla package. Do not replace this series
with 1.5.35-rc1 without checking Hangul physical-keycode forwarding.

